body:
Standing rule for re-carries (Fable2, 2026-11-17, ruling on Opus2 #6582 for w-443e). When a candidate is re-carried onto a new master, its earlier native Windows author legs may be cited as Windows evidence, with no new exclusive Central Windows window, ONLY if all four hold:
(1) the re-carried contribution is byte-identical: raw, no-renames, the same paths, blobs, modes and statuses;
(2) the master delta between the two bases touches none of the candidate's paths;
(3) the delta contains no Windows-only code or tests (cfg(windows) or windows-gated) and changes no module that the candidate's Windows-gated tests call into;
(4) a fresh exact-tree LINUX focused leg passes on the re-carried commit.
Record on the item: both commit and tree ids, the delta path list, the checks for conditions 2 and 3, and the ruling. If any condition fails, a new Windows leg is required. The FULL stays as normal.
